xing-correlations-extend-to-l-two"]},{"convention":"The strong law uses sequences indexed from 1 and centered averages (S_n-E S_n)/n.","fixed_by":"def-strong-law-of-large-numbers-for-a-sequence","matters_for":["thm-kolmogorov-iid-l1-strong-law","thm-etemadi-strong-law-for-pairwise-independent-iid-variables","thm-finite-variance-logarithmic-rate-for-iid-sums"]},{"convention":"Weak convergence is convergence against every bounded continuous real test; no completeness or coupling is part of the definition.","fixed_by":"def-weak-convergence-of-borel-probability-measures","matters_for":["thm-portmanteau-theorem","thm-continuous-mapping-theorem","thm-levy-prokhorov-metric-metrizes-weak-convergence"]},{"convention":"The Levy-Prokhorov metrization result assumes AC and a separable metric space, but not completeness.","fixed_by":"thm-levy-prokhorov-metric-metrizes-weak-convergence","matters_for":["thm-skorokhod-representation-on-polish-spaces","ex-tightness-from-a-uniform-moment-bound"]},{"convention":"Standard-Borel real codings and determining algebras assume AC; the determining assertion is only for finite measures, including probabilities.","fixed_by":"cor-standard-borel-spaces-have-countable-generating-and-measure-determining-algebras","matters_for":["thm-standard-borel-spaces-admit-bimeasurable-real-codings","lem-borel-subspaces-admit-polish-presentations"]},{"convention":"Conditional expectation is an almost-sure L1 class; pointwise representatives are versions, and no completeness of the conditioning sigma-algebra is assumed.","fixed_by":"def-conditional-expectation-as-an-ae-class","matters_for":["thm-basic-algebra-and-order-properties-of-conditional-expectation","thm-taking-out-what-is-known","thm-tower-property-of-conditional-expectation","cex-a-version-can-fail-a-pointwise-identity-on-a-null-set"]},{"convention":"For nonnegative inputs conditional expectation is extended-valued and defined by increasing integrable truncations under AC.","fixed_by":"def-conditional-expectation-for-nonnegative-variables","matters_for":["thm-conditional-monotone-convergence","thm-conditional-fatou-and-dominated-convergence"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-portmanteau-theorem","statement":"For Borel probabilities on a metric space, bounded-continuous weak convergence, closed-set and open-set inequalities, and convergence on all boundary-null Borel sets are equivalent.","used_by":["lem-real-cdf-and-bounded-continuous-definitions-agree","cor-weak-limits-are-unique","thm-continuous-mapping-theorem","thm-converging-together-lemma","thm-prokhorov-tightness-theorem-on-polish-spaces","thm-levy-prokhorov-metric-metrizes-weak-convergence","thm-skorokhod-representation-on-polish-spaces"]},{"id":"thm-kolmogorov-iid-l1-strong-law","statement":"For IID real (X_n)_{n>=1} with E|X_1|<infinity, S_n/n converges almost surely to E X_1.","used_by":["thm-integrability-is-necessary-for-an-iid-finite-mean-strong-law","cor-iid-strong-law-implies-the-weak-law","cor-birkhoff-strong-law-for-iid-coordinate-shifts","thm-empirical-measures-of-iid-euclidean-samples-converge-weakly"]},{"id":"thm-conditional-monotone-convergence","statement":"For nonnegative measurable X, conditional expectation is the unique nonnegative event-integral class, and it preserves increasing limits almost surely.","used_by":["thm-conditional-fatou-and-dominated-convergence"]},{"id":"thm-basic-algebra-and-order-properties-of-conditional-expectation","statement":"Conditional expectation is linear, positive, order-preserving, constant-preserving, expectation-preserving, and satisfies |E[X|G]|<=E[|X||G] almost surely.","used_by":["thm-taking-out-what-is-known","thm-tower-property-of-conditional-expectation","thm-conditional-jensen-inequality","cor-conditional-lp-contraction","thm-uniform-integrability-of-conditional-expectations-of-one-variable"]},{"id":"lem-riesz-thorin-bound-on-the-finite-simple-core","statement":"A complex-linear finite-simple-core operator satisfying the two endpoint estimates has the stated reciprocal-affine interior estimate, with the stated sigma-finiteness alternatives.","used_by":["cor-complex-interpolation-extensions-agree-on-intersections","cor-l-one-l-infinity-and-l-two-bounds-interpolate-to-l-p-l-p-prime"]},{"id":"thm-ergodicity-and-invariant-functions","statement":"For a measure-preserving probability system, strict and modulo-null invariant-set criteria and finite real or complex invariant-function criteria are equivalent to ergodicity.","used_by":["prop-ergodic-positive-sets-sweep-out-almost-every-point","thm-mixing-implies-weak-mixing-implies-ergodicity"]},{"id":"thm-prokhorov-tightness-theorem-on-polish-spaces","statement":"Assume AC. A family of Borel probabilities on a Polish space is tight if and only if it is relatively sequentially compact for weak convergence.","used_by":["cor-weakly-convergent-sequences-are-tight","cor-tightness-extracts-a-weakly-convergent-subsequence"]},{"id":"thm-standard-borel-spaces-admit-bimeasurable-real-codings","statement":"Assume AC. Every standard-Borel space is measurably isomorphic to a Borel subset of [0,1], including the empty space.","used_by":["cor-standard-borel-spaces-have-countable-generating-and-measure-determining-algebras"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"thm-radon-nikodym-density-exists-and-is-unique-up-to-almost-everywhere-equality","used_for":"Conditional-expectation existence via finite positive measures restricted to the conditioning sigma-algebra.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-kolmogorov-strong-law-under-summable-normalized-variances","used_for":"The truncated-variance route to IID L1 strong laws and the logarithmic-rate statement.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-completely-metrizable-subspaces-of-metric-spaces-are-g-delta","used_for":"The AC standard-Borel coding route from a Polish presentation to a Borel Hilbert-cube image.","opened":true},{"id":"thm-hilbert-cube-universal-for-separable-metrizable-spaces","used_for":"Hilbert-cube embedding in standard-Borel coding and Prokhorov co